    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0490" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg402"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1540.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to the
                    Department the naturalization certificate of Assad Kalil Abynemer, born near
                    Beirut, Syria. <pb facs="0491" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/> On examining him he
                    states that he lived in the United States about four years (certificate states
                    eight years); that he is a merchant; that he has had no other paper; has made no
                    declaration of becoming an American citizen; that he bought this paper from a
                    man in New York (he did not know him) who stated that as he was going to Haiti
                    he had better have such document as it would help him in business: that he did
                    not know Mickel Isaac (the witness named in certificate) and that he paid for
                    this paper $50, receiving it as he was about to leave New York in January of the
                    present year.</p>
                <p>I have returned to him the same answer as I have to the others (see No. 1537,
                    September 14, 1904).</p>
                <p>I especially call the attention of the Department to a close examination of the
                    seals that are attached to these documents.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
